  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1145 AM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nUNSEASONABLY WARM AND MOSTLY DRY THROUGH THE WEEKEND: \n\nWith high pressure in place across the Southwest, warm and dry \nconditions will be favored through the weekend. Temperatures \nwill range from 5 to 15 degrees above normal across the region. \nSensible weather will be hard to come by, but some return flow \nfrom a weather system passing over the front range could lead to\nisolated to scattered convection over the San Juans on Sunday \nafternoon. Otherwise, dry conditions persist.\n\nWORK WEEK OUTLOOK: \n\nLooking ahead to next week, high pressure breaks down late \nMonday into Tuesday as a shortwave trough advects through the \nnorthwesterly flow. This could lead to showers and storms over \nthe higher terrain on Tuesday afternoon, but with dry surface \nlevels in place, measurable rainfall could be hard to come by. \nBeyond this week disturbance, high pressure and warm and dry \nconditions remain the name of the game through the work week.",
